HL3 MAIN: footings canonical a0 9.3603e-11, alt a0 1.1312e-10 (the loaders' values, AMENDMENT A1 item 1). kappa = 1/2 FITTED; not theory closed.
law: g = g_N/2 + sqrt(g_N^2/4 + a0 g_N), the inversion of g_N = g^2/(g + a0); rho = log10(g_obs / g_law(g_bar)).

KA5 law inversion
[canonical] g/g_N - 1 at g_N = 1e10 a0: 1.00e-10 (1e9 a0: 1.00e-09); g/sqrt(a0 g_N) - 1 at g_N = 1e-3 a0: 0.0159, 4e-4 a0: 0.0100, 1e-4 a0: 0.0050; round trip g^2/(g + a0) = g_N over 1e-6..1e6 a0: max dev 2.2e-16
[alt] g/g_N - 1 at g_N = 1e10 a0: 1.00e-10 (1e9 a0: 1.00e-09); g/sqrt(a0 g_N) - 1 at g_N = 1e-3 a0: 0.0159, 4e-4 a0: 0.0100, 1e-4 a0: 0.0050; round trip g^2/(g + a0) = g_N over 1e-6..1e6 a0: max dev 4.4e-16
KA5 reading: the high end and the round trip pass. The deep end at exactly g_N = 1e-3 a0 deviates by sqrt(x)/2 = 1.58 % by the law's own exact expansion g = sqrt(a0 g_N) (1 + sqrt(x)/2 + ...); the literal 1 % bar is met from g_N <= 4e-4 a0. The bar as frozen cannot be met by any correct implementation at 1e-3; disclosed, not amended.

